  "Question": "If \\(8\\cdot2^x=5^{y+8},\\) then, when \\(y=-8,\\) \\(x=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-4\\)",
    "B": "\\(-3\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(8\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Substituting \\(y=-8\\) makes the exponent on \\(5\\) zero:\n\\[\n5^{y+8}=5^{-8+8}=5^0=1.\n\\]\nThe equation therefore becomes \\(8\\cdot2^x=1\\), so\n\\[\n2^x=\\frac18=\\frac1{2^3}=2^{-3}.\n\\]\nSince powers of \\(2\\) increase with the exponent, equal values have equal exponents. Thus \\(x=-3\\), choice B.",
